- **Probability of failure (1 - p):** $ \frac{5}{6} $ (probability of rolling something other than 1 on one die roll)

---

### **Applying the Binomial Formula**

The binomial probability formula is:

$$
P(k) = \binom{n}{k} \cdot p^k \cdot (1 - p)^{n - k}
$$

